{#
  driver_table_intro.j2
  =====================
  Text accompanying the full driver-comparison table, which acts as the
  report's reference page. It names exactly which metrics crossed the
  significance threshold so the reader knows what to look for.

  Context variables (from _build_driver_table_ctx):
    has_changes           bool
    scenario_count        int
    multi_scenario        bool
    baseline_name         str
    changed_by_driver     [ { driver, entries: [ { label, direction,
                              magnitude, amount, scope } ] } ]
                          entries are aggregated across the selected scenarios
    changed_driver_names  [str]
    unchanged_drivers     [str]

  NOTE: each list item must render on a single line. Jinja's trim_blocks eats
  the newline that follows a block tag, so lines ending in {% raw %}{% endif %}{% endraw %}
  are terminated with an empty expression to keep the line break.
#}
The table on this page lists every input driver metric side by side, for {{ baseline_name }} and
{{ "each of the " ~ scenario_count ~ " scenarios" if multi_scenario else "the scenario" }} in this report.
It is intended as a reference: the narrative sections that follow discuss only the changes that are large enough to matter.

{% if not has_changes %}
None of the driver metrics differ from {{ baseline_name }} substantially. Any differences in modelled outcomes therefore stem from interactions between drivers rather than from a single dominant change.
{% else %}
The metrics that changed significantly relative to {{ baseline_name }} are grouped by driver below.

{% for group in changed_by_driver %}
- **{{ group.driver }}**: {% for e in group.entries %}{{ e.label }} {{ e.direction }} {{ e.magnitude }}, by {{ e.amount }}{% if e.scope %} ({{ e.scope }}){% endif %}{{ "; " if not loop.last else "." }}{% endfor %}{{ "" }}
{% endfor %}

{% if unchanged_drivers %}
The remaining driver{{ "s" if unchanged_drivers | length != 1 }} ({{ unchanged_drivers | listjoin }}) show{{ "" if unchanged_drivers | length != 1 else "s" }} no significant changes and {{ "are" if unchanged_drivers | length != 1 else "is" }} not discussed further.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
